<%#
  The shell every VibeVic email is rendered into.

  ── Why this looks like 2004 HTML ────────────────────────────────────────
  Because mail clients are 2004 browsers. Outlook on Windows renders through
  Word's engine, which has no flexbox, no grid, no `max-width` on a div worth
  relying on, and no external stylesheets. Tables with explicit widths and
  attributes alongside the CSS are not nostalgia; they are the only layout
  primitive that behaves the same in Apple Mail, Gmail, Outlook and a dozen
  webmails nobody tests against.

  ── Two colour schemes, and why the site has only one ────────────────────
  The product has no dark theme — `index.css` says so, and says why: a dark
  set invented without being validated against a dark surface would be worse
  than none. This is a different question. An email does not choose its
  surroundings: Apple Mail and iOS Mail honour `prefers-color-scheme`, and
  Gmail and Outlook will *forcibly* invert a light email on a dark device
  whether or not it was designed for it. The choice is not "dark mode or no
  dark mode", it is "our dark rendering or theirs", and theirs turns navy text
  on ice into whatever the inversion heuristic produces.

  So the dark palette below is the email's own, derived from the brand hues
  rather than copied from a site theme that does not exist. `color-scheme` and
  `supported-color-schemes` tell the client we have handled it, which is what
  stops most auto-inversion; the media query then does the handling.

  ── Mobile first, because that is where a pitch is read ──────────────────
  600px is the widest this ever gets, and everything inside it is fluid below
  that. Body copy is 16px — smaller and iOS zooms the whole message on its own
  — the buttons are 44px tall, and the padding drops on narrow screens rather
  than the type shrinking.

  ── What is deliberately not here ────────────────────────────────────────
  No images, no web fonts, no tracking pixel. A remote image is a request that
  says the message was opened, and this newsroom does not need to know that
  about anyone. It also means nothing breaks when a client blocks images,
  which most do by default — the design carries in text and colour alone, and
  Fraunces is asked for and gracefully lost to Georgia, which is what a mail
  client will use anyway.
-%>
<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
    <title><%= subject %></title>
    <style>
      /* ── The palette, from the site's own tokens ──────────────────
         Light is `index.css` verbatim: ice ground, navy-ink text,
         blue-grey secondary, bright blue accent. Dark is derived —
         the same hues, the lightness relationship inverted, with the
         accent lifted because 54% blue on a near-black ground is
         darker than it looks on ice. */
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; supported-color-schemes: light dark; }

      body, table, td, a {
        -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
        -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%;
      }
      table { border-collapse: collapse !important; }
      img { border: 0; line-height: 100%; outline: none; text-decoration: none; }

      body {
        margin: 0 !important;
        padding: 0 !important;
        width: 100% !important;
        background-color: #f7fbfd;
      }

      .vv-ground { background-color: #f7fbfd; }
      .vv-card {
        background-color: #ffffff;
        border: 1px solid #d5e2ed;
        border-radius: 12px;
      }
      .vv-rule { background-color: #d5e2ed; }
      .vv-title { color: #111f31; }
      .vv-text { color: #111f31; }
      .vv-muted { color: #4e6480; }
      .vv-accent { color: #1479ea; }
      .vv-bar { background-color: #0e4fa0; }
      .vv-btn {
        background-color: #0e4fa0;
        border: 1px solid #0e4fa0;
        color: #ffffff !important;
      }
      .vv-chip {
        background-color: #e4f2fd;
        color: #0e4fa0;
      }
      .vv-quote {
        border-left: 3px solid #1479ea;
        background-color: #f2f8fd;
      }
      .vv-late { color: #cf2020; }

      /* ── The client's dark mode ────────────────────────────────────
         Only the surfaces and the type move. The accent hue is the
         same blue, lifted in lightness so it clears the ground it now
         sits on rather than sinking into it. */
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        body, .vv-ground { background-color: #0b141f !important; }
        .vv-card {
          background-color: #121e2c !important;
          border-color: #26374b !important;
        }
        .vv-rule { background-color: #26374b !important; }
        .vv-title, .vv-text { color: #e8f1f8 !important; }
        .vv-muted { color: #9db0c6 !important; }
        .vv-accent { color: #63aef7 !important; }
        .vv-bar { background-color: #1479ea !important; }
        .vv-btn {
          background-color: #1479ea !important;
          border-color: #1479ea !important;
          color: #ffffff !important;
        }
        .vv-chip {
          background-color: #17304d !important;
          color: #a9cffb !important;
        }
        .vv-quote {
          border-left-color: #63aef7 !important;
          background-color: #16273a !important;
        }
        .vv-late { color: #ff8a80 !important; }
      }

      /* ── Narrow screens ───────────────────────────────────────────
         The padding gives way, never the type size. A pitch read on a
         phone at 13px is a pitch read badly. */
      @media only screen and (max-width: 620px) {
        .vv-pad { padding-left: 20px !important; padding-right: 20px !important; }
        .vv-shell { padding: 16px 8px !important; }
        .vv-h1 { font-size: 22px !important; line-height: 30px !important; }
        .vv-btn-cell a { display: block !important; text-align: center !important; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body class="vv-ground">
    <%#
      The preheader: the grey line a phone shows under the subject. Left
      unset it fills with whatever the first words of the body happen to be,
      which on a pitch is the covering line's "Hello". Given one, it is the
      second sentence a recipient reads. The spacer characters after it stop
      the client from padding it out with the body anyway.
    -%>
    <div style="display:none;font-size:1px;color:#f7fbfd;line-height:1px;max-height:0;max-width:0;opacity:0;overflow:hidden;">
      <%= preheader %>
      <%- '&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;'.repeat(60) %>
    </div>

    <table role="presentation" class="vv-ground" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" class="vv-shell" style="padding: 32px 16px;">

          <table role="presentation" class="vv-card" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px;max-width:600px;">
            <%# The brand bar. Four pixels of ink navy, which is the whole of
                the identity that survives an image-blocking client. -%>
            <tr>
              <td class="vv-bar" height="4" style="height:4px;line-height:4px;font-size:4px;border-radius:12px 12px 0 0;">&nbsp;</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="vv-pad" style="padding: 28px 36px 8px 36px;">
                <p class="vv-muted" style="margin:0;font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.4px;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;">
                  VibeVic Newsroom
                </p>
                <h1 class="vv-h1 vv-title" style="margin:10px 0 0 0;font-family:'Fraunces',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;line-height:33px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
                  <%= heading %>
                </h1>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="vv-pad" style="padding: 18px 36px 30px 36px;font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:26px;">
                <%- body %>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="vv-pad" style="padding: 0 36px;">
                <div class="vv-rule" style="height:1px;line-height:1px;font-size:1px;">&nbsp;</div>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="vv-pad" style="padding: 18px 36px 28px 36px;">
                <p class="vv-muted" style="margin:0;font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:19px;">
                  <%= footnote %>
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>

        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
